From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:37:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: refuse automation paths through AmigaDOS links

Problem: on x86_64 ABIv11 (pool v11-2) the MCP acceptance client made a soft
  link inside the write root (MakeLink "RAM:pc/mcp work/escape-link"
  RAM:pcoutside). doc_open through it read RAM:pcoutside/secret.png and
  doc_save wrote RAM:pcoutside/new.png: the symlink check added for builds
  without cap-std never fired, because AROS's lstat() follows soft links.
Rationale: a link is visible only in its parent's directory entry, so the
  new photocraft-aros-fs crate walks the existing components with
  Examine/ExNext and refuses soft and hard links (ST_SOFTLINK, ST_LINKDIR,
  ST_LINKFILE). Missing components end the walk. Still a check before the
  operation, not confinement; the CLI's stderr warning says so.
Scope: cfg(target_os = "aros"); new crate crates/aros-fs (C via build.rs,
  same compiler/SDK handling as the shell).
Upstream-status: local-only.
Prerequisites: 0008 (symlink refusal), 0010 (photocraft-aros-stdin wiring).
Verification: guest MCP run (link-read-refused, link-write-refused).
Removal: when cap-std (or std's lstat) works for AROS links.
